Upgraded from version 6.8.1 to version 6.8.2


----------------------------------------------------------------

Date: Fri Oct 30 2026

Version=6.8.2
Release=3

Synopsis:
Add native, session-local window tab groups for server-decorated applications.
Provide a tabbed decoration, Window Tabs menu, separate grouping/tab shortcuts,
and shared geometry, tiling and window state. Preserve Alt+Tab and its selected
effect. Include integration coverage and WINDOW-TABS.md usage instructions.

----------------------------------------------------------------

Date: Fri Oct 30 2026

Version=6.8.2
Release=4

Synopsis:
Move window tab controls into More Actions -> Tab Windows. List eligible open
windows by title and icon for direct grouping, with safe handling of closed or
changed targets. Keep tab shortcuts and the existing Alt+Tab effect.

----------------------------------------------------------------

Date: Fri Oct 30 2026

Version=6.8.2
Release=5

Synopsis:
Keep every existing tab when adding another window or merging tab groups.
Check size and decoration compatibility across all members before merging.
Cover adding third/fourth windows from either menu, group merging, rejection
of incompatible hidden tabs, and real Kate/Konsole/KWrite grouping.

----------------------------------------------------------------

Date: Sat Oct 31 2026

Version=6.8.2
Release=6

Synopsis:
Keep all tabbed applications visible and activatable in the taskbar, including
Xwayland tabs across minimize/restore. Preserve normal pinned-launcher merging,
explicit skip-taskbar rules, and the existing Alt+Tab group behavior.
Add a three-window, one-pinned-application regression using Plasma's taskbar model.

----------------------------------------------------------------

Date: Sun Nov 1 2026

Version=6.8.2
Release=7

Synopsis:
Identify existing tab groups by all member titles in the Tab Windows menu,
for example Group: Turnover Golf + Kasts. Keep a stable label when selecting
a different tab. Preserve whole-group joining and the release 6 taskbar fix.
Cover combined labels, literal ampersands, and adding third/fourth windows.

----------------------------------------------------------------

Date: Sun Nov 1 2026

Version=6.8.2
Release=8

Synopsis:
Automatically remember normal windows' virtual desktop, monitor, geometry,
restored size and maximized state. Restore tab groups, tab order and selected
tab when applications reopen. No settings switches or manual save required.
Match multiple windows by application, role and title; respect window rules
and keep windows visible when a monitor or desktop is removed. Save atomically
and freeze the layout before logout closes applications. Keep the release 6
per-application taskbar behavior and release 7 combined group menu labels.
Add integration coverage for restoration, grouping and session lifecycle.

----------------------------------------------------------------

Date: Sun Nov 1 2026

Version=6.8.2
Release=9

Synopsis:
Separate automatic layout memory into kwin-window-layout-memory.patch,
applied after kwin-window-tabs.patch. Keep tabbing, group menu labels and
taskbar behavior in the tab patch. Add separate layout-memory documentation.
Both patches together produce the identical compiled and tested release 8
source; no runtime behavior or settings changes.

----------------------------------------------------------------

Date: Sun Nov 1 2026

Version=6.8.2
Release=10

Synopsis:
Fix the KWin session D-Bus state mapping to match Plasma's normal/saving/quitting
values, so logout cannot resume recording and erase groups as apps close.
Remember tab membership until explicit detach, including when every app closes.
Reunite any available members in either launch order; later members join in saved
order without launching other applications. Preserve closed members when merging
groups and pruning window history. Keep all changes in the separate layout-memory
patch, with the window-tabs patch unchanged. Add lifecycle integration regressions
and verify close/reopen plus logout/login using isolated production compositors.

